      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): explain replace-mode filtering in model picker",
        "body": "Closes #104545\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `models.mode: \"replace\"` filters the model catalog, the Control UI showed the resulting models without explaining why other bundled or discovered models might be absent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nConfigured model-list responses now carry additive `catalogMode: \"replace\"` metadata. The chat model picker and Quick Settings use that metadata to explain that model settings are filtering the catalog, without claiming that every visible row was explicitly configured. Full-catalog (`view: \"all\"`) responses do not carry the hint metadata.\n\nThe picker action opens the Models section directly at `/settings/ai-agents?section=models#config-section-models`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can tell that local model settings are filtering the catalog and can navigate directly to the relevant settings instead of treating an absent model as an upstream support problem.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `main` at `f167089d617`; exact pushed head: `b728e655c9f`.\n- GitHub reports the pushed head mergeable after resolving the gateway schema and chat-pane import conflicts against current architecture.\n- Focused Gateway and UI regressions: 5 files, 272 tests passed.\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-methods/models.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/models.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-state.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/pages/config/quick.test.ts`\n- Targeted Chromium replace-mode regression: 1 passed, 6 skipped.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts -t 'explains model filtering in replace mode'`\n- `pnpm protocol:check` passed with generated outputs stable.\n- Focused `oxfmt` passed for all 19 changed TypeScript/CSS files; type-aware `oxlint` passed for all 17 changed TypeScript files.\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports` passed with the current repository baseline of 2592 entries.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- The final locale diff changes only `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts`; generated non-English locale files remain on the repository workflow.\n- Fresh local `codex review --base origin/main` on the rebased diff found no concrete regression in the gateway/UI flow or route target.\n- Exact-head desktop 1280x900 and mobile 393x852 renders passed and were visually inspected. Both show the replace-mode hint and Manage models action with clean wrapping and no overlap; they match the immutable screenshots in the earlier proof comment.\n\nBefore: the UI overclaimed that replace mode showed only models explicitly listed in Settings.\n\nAfter: the picker and Quick Settings state, \"Replace mode filters models according to your model settings,\" and link directly to the Models settings section.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex was used to implement, test, and review this change. No agent transcript is attached.\n",
        "branch": "agent/model-picker-replace-mode-hint",
